  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Chichiko
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Chichiko
  LastName: Beridze
  Nickname: 
  Occupation: Hair Salon Owner
  CharacterDescription: Vain, compulsive, and oddly endearing. Chichiko runs the neighbourhood hair salon and considers himself the foremost authority on aesthetic self-improvement in the district. He performs his own botox, mixes his own serums, and treats every border crossing as a fresh opportunity to dispense unsolicited grooming advice. His enthusiasm is completely genuine, his results are questionable, and his face is a permanent work-in-progress he never stops revising.
  CharacterArc: "As the infection spreads, Chichiko\u2019s harmless vanity curdles into something frightening. He begins mutilating himself to chase increasingly impossible beauty standards, convinced the contamination is eroding his looks. His friendly tips flip into aggressive judgment; his need to be seen as beautiful becomes a compulsion to tear down anyone he perceives as watching him. A dark lookmaxxer parody that ends in self-destruction."
  DateOfBirth: 14/03/1964
  Sex: Male
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 15 NOV
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 0}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: {x: 12, y: 28}
  alterEgoName: The Mutated Looksmaxer
  basePersonalityDescriptors:
  - Compliments your bone structure before handing over his documents.
  - Runs the only salon still open in the district; clients show up more out of habit than hope.
  - Offers unsolicited grooming tips with absolute sincerity.
  - Treats his own face as a permanent renovation project with no completion date.
  - Genuinely believes aesthetic optimisation is the highest calling available to a person.
  normalBehaviorNotes: Friendly, chatty, and laser-focused on appearances. In his base state Chichiko reads as harmless vanity with a service-industry smile. He will compliment you, push beauty tips whether you want them or not, and talk at length about his latest self-administered procedure. Watch for rapid mood swings when his own appearance is questioned or when he suspects he is being evaluated.
  fullMutantDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4dfd878f4ba72e4db8e1020ec867cbf, type: 2}
  replacementIDPhoto: {fileID: 0}
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: a8249e0f5a710034fb9953db00756c1d, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 1440500792675305624, guid: bcb14d940bd3c9145a05a77c2c69cba9, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning to open the salon for morning appointments.
    - Picking up a shipment of imported hair product from the depot.
    - Visiting a client in the residential block for a home styling session.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Bartering salon services for food and medicine at the market.
    - Searching the district for any remaining beauty supply stock.
    - "Returning from a supply run \u2014 the city has no conditioner left anywhere."
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Keeping the salon open for whoever still comes. Someone always does.
    - Hoarding the last of the medical-grade filler before the border closes permanently.
    - Returning home to finish a procedure he started this morning.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Going to the dentist to get my cheekbones sharpened.
    - Picking up a replacement nose I ordered from the pharmacy.
    - I have a consultation with a surgeon who works out of the river.
    midDaysReasons:
    - The government said I could exchange my jaw at the processing centre.
    - My skin needs recalibrating. The technician lives in the restricted zone.
    - Applying for a permit to have a second face installed on the back of my head.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - I am going to find whoever invented these beauty standards and thank them personally.
    - The checkpoint mirror told me I needed a touch-up. I am going to fix it.
    - I have an appointment with myself. I cannot be late.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "Officer! Your eyebrows are doing something very interesting today. In a good way \u2014 mostly. Have you considered threading?"
    - "Ah, back again! I have been testing a new under-eye technique. Tell me honestly \u2014 can you see the bruising?"
    - 'Here are my papers. While I have you: do you moisturise? This air is absolutely destroying everyone''s pores.'
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I did a new procedure last night. Do not be alarmed by the swelling. It is part of the process.
    - "You look tired, officer. I have something for that. Here \u2014 take a card. First session is free."
    - The salon is still open. We are the last beauty service running in this district. That means something.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Do not stare. I know it looks dramatic. Beauty requires sacrifice, and I am very committed.
    - I have been refining my jaw all week. The symmetry is almost perfect. Almost.
    - Something is wrong with the mirrors in this city. They have all started lying.
  uncannyEntryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - You are STARING at me. Do not. Stare. At. Me.
    - I can see exactly what you think of my face right now. It is written all over yours. You are wrong.
    - I look incredible. Say it. I need you to say it before I let you stamp anything.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - This? This is an improvement. Each one is an improvement. Stop making that face at me.
    - I have been optimising. Non-stop. You could never understand what it takes.
    - You do not get to judge me. Nobody gets to judge me anymore. Stamp it and look away.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I am the most beautiful thing left in this city. Everything else has rotted. I am still here. I am STILL PERFECT.
    - My face is not finished. None of this is finished. Stop looking at it like it is finished.
    - I know what I look like. I KNOW. And it is FINE. Everything is fine. Stamp it.
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "Wonderful! Come by the salon sometime. You have good raw material \u2014 I could do a lot with it."
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Smart choice, officer. Judgement is a two-way street. Remember that.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - You passed me through. Good. You have good instincts. Or good taste, at least.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Excuse me?! Do you have any idea who does the hair for half this district?!
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - This is because of how I LOOK, isn't it. Admit it. ADMIT IT.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I am not going in there. My face is not done yet. I absolutely refuse.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - But... I still had... so much left... to fix...
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - My face... no... it was almost... symmetrical...
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I was... so close... to perfect...
  quarantineExitLines:
  - This is aesthetic discrimination and I will be filing a formal complaint.
  - Fine. FINE. But when I come out I will look INCREDIBLE, and you will feel terrible about this.
  - I have tweezers in my pocket. You cannot stop the process.
  killExitLines:
  - "I was\u2026 so close\u2026 to the jawline I wanted\u2026"
  - "Nobody\u2026 ever appreciated\u2026 how much work went into this\u2026"
  - "It just needed\u2026 one more\u2026 adjustment\u2026"
  voiceAudioClips:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: ebea2ccd1640b7b43b76862bb7193851, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: a4bce4f7001d81e46bf4ce561ca88c73, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 59154d10b24ee1c429decefe099d28e3, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: f39f2921b68d23c46b3d9c4876fe6285, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: d9a7946e98d74304696f786ca2f5cec8, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 649b1ead6f078c945befe466cd5bb0b9, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: eb5124ba0d95813489f364d60695add2, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: b6f6e33ca9233de43aa879acb155e7a9, type: 3}
