  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7e1f790693c494d449c01897a975fc1a, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The salon on Rustaveli. Two perms, a colour, and my own jaw between clients. Exhausting, but worth it.
    midDaysAnswer: The market by the river. I traded a haircut for filler from a man with Polish labels. Do not tell anyone.
    finalDaysAnswer: The salon. I keep it open for whoever still comes. And I was working on myself. I lost track of the hours.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My salon on Plekhanov Avenue. Small place, but the light is good for colour work.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The barracks canteen. I cut hair for the soldiers now. The salon closed weeks ago, like all the others.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Home. I shut the salon for good last month. There is no one left worth cutting.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: The supply depot. They still have what I need. Do not ask what. You would not understand the list.
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: From the mirror. I have been working on myself. Non-stop. It is a full-time commitment and I do not expect you to understand.
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: I do not remember leaving. I was in the mirror for a long time. Time moves differently when you are focused.
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Bruising along the jaw. Self-administered filler, last Thursday. It settles by Sunday. I have done this twelve times.
    midDaysAnswer: Some swelling. A little numbness in the cheeks. My pain threshold has gone up, which I take as a very good sign.
    finalDaysAnswer: I cannot feel my cheekbones. I sleep badly. Neither matters. The proportions are finally correct.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nothing. I have never had a procedure in my life, officer. This is all natural. Good genes.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No swelling at all. A surgeon at the polyclinic did my last injection. Very professional, very clean.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I feel wonderful. I stopped all procedures a month ago. I have not touched my face since.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: I told you. No symptoms. These are improvements. There is a significant difference.
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: Everyone keeps calling them symptoms. They are not symptoms. They are upgrades.
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: My body is cooperating fully with the vision. That is all you need to know.
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Your skin is dehydrated, officer. Drink water. Use SPF. I am genuinely begging you.
    - I opened the salon at six this morning. I will close it when the city does.
    - A man came in yesterday asking for the post-apocalyptic look. I gave him a trim and sent him home.
    midDays:
    - The good products are all gone from the shelves. I have been improvising. The results are mostly fine.
    - People keep telling me I look different. I look optimised. There is a difference.
    - Certain fillers can still be sourced from the medical quarter if you know the right people. I know the right people.
    finalDays:
    - The mirror in my salon cracked this morning. I took it as a challenge.
    - Everyone in this city has stopped caring about how they look. It is deeply upsetting to witness.
    - I am not finished. I want to be clear about that. What you are seeing is a work in progress.
    uncannyEarlyDays:
    - Stop looking at my face. I can see you looking.
    - I know what I look like. I am the only one who gets to decide what that means.
    uncannyMidDays:
    - You have an opinion about my face. I can tell. Keep it to yourself.
    - I rate everyone I meet on sight. You are not performing as well as you think you are.
    uncannyFinalDays:
    - Perfect. Almost perfect. Getting closer every single day.
    - I am the last beautiful thing left in this district. Someone has to be.
  IDNumber: 4819263
